From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: dts: ingenic: t41: put the pinctrl states on the mainline binding

The stock T41 pinctrl tree uses the vendor form: each state node carries
ingenic,pinmux/ingenic,pinmux-funcsel. The mainline pinctrl-ingenic
driver parses function/groups, so every consumer fails with
"there are no valid maps for state default".

Rewrite every leaf group as function/groups, taking the function name
from the driver's t41 group table. The label names are unchanged, so
existing pinctrl-0 references keep working. The i2c2 group node names
are corrected to the driver's hyphenated spelling; labels stay as-is.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
